### Naming Conventions

- **Components**: PascalCase `.tsx` (`AllApplicationsPage.tsx`, `DataTable.tsx`).
- **Hooks**: camelCase with `use` prefix (`useApplications.ts`).
- **Utils / API / stores**: camelCase `.ts` (`http.ts`, `provider-account.ts`).
- **Types**: PascalCase (`Application`, `LandscapeEnvironment`).
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE.
- **Route names**: kebab-case strings (`all-applications`, `selected-landscape`).

## Component Patterns

### Component Structure

```tsx
import { useMemo, useState } from 'react';
import { useNavigate } from 'react-router';
import { toast } from 'sonner';

import { parseApiError } from '@/api/http';
import { PageHeader } from '@/components/PageHeader';
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { useApplications } from '@/hooks/useApplications';
import type { Application } from '@/types/cmdb';

type AllApplicationsPageProps = {
  /** optional props when needed */
};

export default function AllApplicationsPage(_props: AllApplicationsPageProps) {
  const navigate = useNavigate();
  const { data, isLoading, refetch } = useApplications(false);
  const [search, setSearch] = useState('');

  const filtered = useMemo(() => {
    /* … */
    return data ?? [];
  }, [data, search]);

  async function handleRefresh(): Promise<void> {
    try {
      await refetch();
    } catch (err) {
      toast.error(await parseApiError(err));
    }
  }

  if (isLoading) return <div className="p-6">Loading…</div>;

  return (
    <div>
      <PageHeader title="Applications" onRefresh={handleRefresh} />
      {/* … */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Component Rules

- Function components only; typed props via `type` (not untyped `props`).
- Default export for page components; named exports for shared components when
  multiple exports exist in one file.
- Server state in TanStack Query hooks — not inline `useEffect` + axios in
  pages unless there is a one-off reason.
- UI state (search text, sheet open, form drafts) stays local with `useState`.
- User-facing errors always go through `parseApiError` + `toast` (sonner).
- Confirms/deactivates use `ConfirmDialog` (AlertDialog), not `window.confirm`.

## Data Fetching Patterns

### TanStack Query hooks

Domain hooks live in `src/hooks/` and wrap `src/api/cmdb.ts`:

```ts
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';

import * as cmdb from '@/api/cmdb';

export const applicationsQueryKey = (includeInactive: boolean) =>
  ['applications', includeInactive] as const;

export function useApplications(includeInactive = false) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: applicationsQueryKey(includeInactive),
    queryFn: () => cmdb.listApplications(includeInactive),
  });
}
```

After mutations (create/update/deactivate), invalidate related query keys via
`queryClient.invalidateQueries`.

### API response normalization

`src/api/cmdb.ts` exports per-resource functions that wrap `api.get/post/patch/delete`
and normalize list responses with `normalizeListResponse<T>` so the UI tolerates
`Array | { items } | { data } | { results }` shapes from the backend.

## API Layer Patterns

### `src/api/http.ts`

```ts
export const api = createClient(); // axios with VITE_API_BASE_URL

export function registerAuthorizationGetter(fn: () => string | null): void;
export function register401Handler(fn: () => Promise<boolean>): void;
export async function parseApiError(err: unknown): Promise<string>;
```

- Authorization header is set per-request from a getter registered in `main.tsx`.
  Do **not** import the auth store inside `http.ts` (avoids circular deps).
- `parseApiError` is the single source of user-facing error messages.

### `src/api/cmdb.ts`

Conventions:

- List endpoints take `includeInactive: boolean` first; pass through
  `inactiveParam(...)`.
- List endpoints normalize with `normalizeListResponse<T>`.
- Mutations return resource shape `T`; deletes return `void`.

### URL & base path

- Browser base URL: `import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL` (default `/api`).
- Dev proxy: `vite.config.ts` proxies `/api` → `VITE_DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET`.

## State Management Patterns

### Zustand auth store

Auth/session lives in `src/stores/auth.ts`. Use selector helpers exported from
the store (`selectIsLoggedIn`, `selectIsAdmin`, `selectCanManageApplications`,
`selectAuthorizationHeader`) rather than reading raw state in guards.

```ts
const isLoggedIn = useAuthStore((s) => selectIsLoggedIn(s));
```

Thin wrapper `useAuth.ts` is optional; prefer direct Zustand selectors in
components and route guards.

### Server state vs UI state

| Concern | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Auth / session | Zustand (`stores/auth.ts`) |
| Server data (lists, details) | TanStack Query (`hooks/use*.ts`) |
| UI-only (search, modals, drafts) | Local `useState` in the component |

## Type System Patterns

All domain types live in `src/types/cmdb.ts`:

- Use `type` over `interface`.
- String unions for finite enums (`DataClass`, `ResourceScope`); hosting provider codes are lookup-backed strings.
- Prefer const-object pattern over TypeScript `enum`.
- Never use `any`. Use `unknown` at boundaries and narrow.
- Explicit return types on exported functions.

## Routing Patterns

### Routes (`src/router/index.tsx`)

- Public: `/login`, `/auth/callback`.
- Authenticated tree under `AppShell`: Discover + Management pages.
- Route names are kebab-case strings.
- Lazy-loaded pages wrapped in `<Suspense>`.

### Auth guards

1. Hydrate session before first protected navigation (`HydrateAuth` layout).
2. Unauthenticated → `/login?redirect=<fullPath>`. Never bounce logout straight
   to Cognito `/oauth2/authorize`.
3. `meta.admin` without `isAdmin` → Discover Applications.
4. `meta.appEdit` without `canManageApplications` → Discover Applications.
5. Logged-in user hitting `/login` → Discover Applications.

## Styling Patterns

- Tailwind utility classes in JSX; use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` to merge classes.
- Design tokens in `src/index.css`: primary `#0f766e`, header `#134e4a`,
  surface `#f1f5f9`.
- shadcn primitives in `components/ui/` — do not put feature logic there.
- IBM Plex Sans loaded in `index.html`.

## Testing Patterns

- **Vitest** with **happy-dom**.
- Colocated tests in `__tests__/` adjacent to source (`stores/__tests__/auth.test.ts`).
- CI: `npm run test:unit:ci`.
- Ported tests cover auth, cognito, http, provider-account utils; extend with
  router guard and DataTable smoke tests as needed.

## Import Patterns

Prettier import order (`@trivago/prettier-plugin-sort-imports`):

1. `react` and `react-*`
2. Third-party modules
3. `@/api/*`, `@/stores/*`, `@/router/*`, `@/hooks/*`
4. `@/pages/*`, `@/components/*`, `@/lib/*`, `@/utils/*`, `@/types/*`, `@/assets/*`

Use `@/` alias exclusively under `src/` — avoid `../../` climbs.

## Error Handling Patterns

```ts
try {
  await cmdb.createApplication(body);
  toast.success('Application created.');
} catch (err) {
  toast.error(await parseApiError(err));
}
```

- 401 handler in `main.tsx`: Basic → clear session + `/login`; Cognito → try
  refresh, else clear session + `/login` (no Cognito logout on expired refresh).
- Explicit Log out: Cognito → hosted UI logout URL; Basic → `/login`.

## Authentication Patterns

### Auth modes

`VITE_AUTH_MODE`: `basic` | `cognito` | `both` (default `both`).

- **Basic**: username/password → `GET /me` with Basic header → role in sessionStorage.
- **Cognito**: PKCE hosted UI, callback, refresh leeway (60s), 30s refresh tick
  in `AppShell`.
- Roles: `admin` | `app_editor` | `viewer` from `custom:roles` /
  `cognito:groups` using `VITE_ADMIN_ROLE_CLAIM_VALUE` and
  `VITE_APP_EDIT_ROLE_CLAIM_VALUE`.

### Authorization header injection

`main.tsx` registers the getter:

```ts
registerAuthorizationGetter(() =>
  selectAuthorizationHeader(useAuthStore.getState()),
);
```

Do **not** import the auth store inside `src/api/http.ts`.

## Environment & Deployment

### Environment Variables

Build-time (Vite `import.meta.env`):

- `VITE_API_BASE_URL` — runtime API base path (default `/api`).
- `VITE_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH` — app base path (default `/`).
- `VITE_DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET` — dev-only proxy target.
- `VITE_AUTH_MODE`, `VITE_COGNITO_*`, `VITE_ADMIN_ROLE_CLAIM_VALUE`,
  `VITE_APP_EDIT_ROLE_CLAIM_VALUE`.

See `.env.example` for the full list.

GitHub Environments (`sb`, `dev`, `tst`, `prod`) define AWS deploy vars and
runtime config. Cognito build-time vars are wired through
`argus-build-manual-any.yml`.

### Deploy Workflows

- `argus-build-manual-any.yml` — `workflow_dispatch`; pick environment + ref;
  OIDC role; `npm run build:${env}`; S3 sync; CloudFront invalidate.
- `quality-auto-report.yml` — ESLint, `tsc`, Vitest, build on PR/push to
  `main`; comments SPA quality summary on PRs.
- `tag-commit.yml` — manual sprint tag `vYYYY.SS.N`.

### Local POC deploy

`npm run deploy:poc` (`scripts/deploy-poc.mjs` + `.env.deploy.poc`) for ad-hoc
pushes. Prefer GitHub Actions for shared environments.

## Code Quality Rules

- `strict: true`, no `any`, explicit return types on exports.
- ESLint: `eslint-plugin-react-hooks`, `eslint-plugin-react-refresh`,
  `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`: error.
- Single quotes, semicolons, 80-col print width (Prettier).
- Boolean names: `isX`, `hasX`, `canX`, `shouldX`.
- Prefer early returns and immutable updates.

## Best Practices Checklist

When adding a feature or page:

- [ ] Function component with typed props; server state via Query hooks.
- [ ] Imports use `@/` alias.
- [ ] Network calls through `src/api/cmdb.ts`, not ad-hoc axios.
- [ ] Errors via `parseApiError` + sonner toasts.
- [ ] Loading and error UI handled.
- [ ] Route guards updated in `src/router/index.tsx` if needed.
- [ ] New env vars added to `.env.example` and deploy workflow.
- [ ] Run `lint`, `type-check`, `test:unit:ci` before push.
